wlan: sample the MCU right after the WLAN READY bit

M88: the READY bit now rises and the WLAN probe completes, but a few
hundred milliseconds later the MCU stops answering the driver-own
handshake (WHLPCR bit 8 never returns) and the scan times out.  This is
diagnostic only: right after READY the patch reads the MCU state once,
tries one driver-own handshake, releases it again and then samples
cpupcr/WHLPCR/WCIR five times, 200 ms apart.  That tells whether the
firmware is still running (cpupcr moves) or has already halted.

Controlled by t1100_post_ready (default 0: the extra handshake and
register reads disturb the firmware and lead to FW_OWN_INVALID_ACCESS
storms, so the block must stay off in normal operation).
--- a/common/wlan_lib.c
+++ b/common/wlan_lib.c
@@ -966,6 +966,10 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(t1100_start_addr,
 		 "T1100: start the firmware at this address only (0 = default sequence)");
 static int t1100_ready_trace;
+static int t1100_post_ready;
+module_param(t1100_post_ready, int, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(t1100_post_ready,
+		 "T1100: dump the MCU state right after the WLAN READY bit");
 module_param(t1100_ready_trace, int, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(t1100_ready_trace,
 		 "T1100: print cpupcr while waiting for the WLAN READY bit");
@@ -1464,6 +1468,22 @@
 			if (t1100_readback)
 				t1100_mem_dump(prAdapter, 0x000a5800, 4, "after-start");
 
+			/* T1100 M88: what does the MCU do right after READY? */
+			if (fgReady && t1100_post_ready) {
+				BOOLEAN fgOwn;
+				int i4K;
+
+				t1100_hif_state(prAdapter, "post-ready-0");
+				fgOwn = nicpmSetDriverOwn(prAdapter);
+				pr_info("t1100-post: driver own right after READY -> %d\n", fgOwn);
+				if (fgOwn)
+					nicpmSetFWOwn(prAdapter, FALSE);
+				for (i4K = 0; i4K < 5; i4K++) {
+					kalMsleep(200);
+					t1100_hif_state(prAdapter, "post-ready-later");
+				}
+			}
+
 			if (fgReady == FALSE && t1100_warm_reset && !t1100_redownloaded) {
 				/* T1100 M55: the warm reset wipes the MCU RAM, so the
 				 * RAM image must be downloaded again before a second
